Drop a doc comment that contradicts the code it documents.

The block comment on _audio_filters_get_filters() says of the aresample
segment:

    (in this source the condition is written as never taken; adjust if you
     re-enable rate mismatch handling here)

The condition is taken.  It reads

    if ((self->iavctx->sample_rate != self->oavctx->sample_rate) &&
        str_snprintf(sample_rate, sizeof(sample_rate), "aresample=%d",
                     self->oavctx->sample_rate))
        return -1;

so "aresample=<rate>" is emitted whenever the input and output sample rates
differ -- which is the normal case for any profile that resamples.  The note
presumably survived an earlier revision where the segment was stubbed out.

Documentation only; no generated filter string changes.

Reported upstream against PR #2117.

--- src/transcoding/transcode/audio.c.orig
+++ src/transcoding/transcode/audio.c
@@ -160,9 +160,8 @@ _audio_requires_asetpts(TVHContext *self)
  *
  * Pieces (in join order):
  * - @c asetpts=N/SR/TB — normalizes PTS on the audio link (sample rate / time base).
- * - Optional @c aresample=@<output_sample_rate@> when input and output sample rates
- *   differ (in this source the condition is written as never taken; adjust if you
- *   re-enable rate mismatch handling here).
+ * - Optional @c aresample=@<output_sample_rate@> when input and output sample
+ *   rates differ.
  * - Optional @c aformat=… when input and output differ in @c sample_fmt and/or
  *   channel count: adds @c sample_fmts=… and/or @c channel_layouts=… as required
  *   by the @c aformat filter.
